//@ compile-fail
//@ error-contains: `@allow` does not recognise this warning; the warnings are: stale_write
//
// A misspelled `@allow` that silently suppressed nothing would look exactly like a
// suppression that worked, so the name must be one the compiler actually emits — and
// the error lists the choices, which today is a list of one.

@allow(stale_wrote)
fn main() {}
